{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/358652-is-it-at-all-possible-for-hunters-to-have-supernatural-allies","id":358652,"title":"Is it at all possible for Hunters to have supernatural allies?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-03T17:31:51-08:00","id":358652,"title":"Is it at all possible for Hunters to have supernatural allies?","content":"I apologize in advance if this sounds like a stupid question. I just think some Hunters could find uses for supernatural allies. Changelings can swear power boosting pledges and give goblin fruit, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T17:59:48-08:00","id":358681,"title":"","content":"Absolutely, according to compacts and conspiracies, there are long night members who actively seek to become supernaturals, Cheiron has witch and vampire snitches they pay in thaumatech, and the AO is working on making their own prometheans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T18:29:48-08:00","id":358690,"title":"","content":"Totally. In addition to tier one cells which are by definition going to be very diverse and dependent on the circumstances of the individual hunters, pretty much every compact or conspiracy in the corebook, and most of the ones in the supplements, are broad enough to contain factions amenable to cooperating with more benign supernaturals against shared enemies. The Lucifuge itself is pretty much an entire conspiracy of hunters who blur the line between man and monster themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T19:06:40-08:00","id":358720,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Compact/Conspiracy and the Supernaturals, really; I could see a few different Cells having a Ghoul ally, while a Cainite would probably murder them as a matter of course.<br /> <br /> Really, it depends on whether or not the Hunters can keep their <i>overpowering</i> zealotry on a leash.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-03T20:20:18-08:00","id":358770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GottaGoFeast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/358652-is-it-at-all-possible-for-hunters-to-have-supernatural-allies#post358652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize in advance if this sounds like a stupid question. I just think some Hunters could find uses for supernatural allies. Changelings can swear power boosting pledges and give goblin fruit, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my experience with Hunter, I find that particular situation a bit unlikely mostly because unless a Hunter knew a Changeling could perform power boosting pledges in advance and coerced a Changeling into it, they would never have an opportunity to utilize it. Granted all things have an exception, but I see this sort of situation as more Changeling than Hunter initiated. Such as a Changeling enlisting the help of Hunters to help take down his Fetch and granting them powers to do so.<br /> <br /> HOWEVER!!! That does not mean that Hunters can't have supernatural allies and I actually see them using them as allies fairly frequently, especially in Tier 1 or 2 games. A very possible scenario is hunters going to kill some sort of Vampire that has been using a local nightclub as a feeding ground. Hunters naturally want to end the Vampires life because well...they don't understand that the vampire doesn't want to kill the humans, only borrow some blood here and there. In the meantime, the hunters find out that the vampire has actually been ruthlessly driving our other supernaturals from the area as it attempts to make itself a secure haven.<br /> <br /> Obviously the Hunters are intrigued by this information and offer an alliance with the vampire after a bit of internal deliberation. The hunters will protect the vampire during daylight hours, and in return, the Vampire provides as much information and even helps the Hunters take out some of the more annoying supernatural foes that appear that the Hunters would have had an extremely hard time dealing with just by themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T12:56:28-08:00","id":361515,"title":"","content":"There was a fairly big mention in Mortal Remains about interactions between Demons and Hunters. Based a little on that, I'd say that most other Supernaturals have similar interactions at times. There are various ways they could be allies of Hunters.<br /> <br /> While Conspiracies have ways to detect various Supernaturals, Cells probably don't have anything that's completely reliable. They might be fighting alongside a monster and not even know it. It's a great plan for the Supernatural, because you can direct a bunch mortals, already in the know, against your enemies. Maybe that monster is just a patron, providing resources and intel, and suddenly the fight is looking up. Hell, maybe they fight right alongside you. most look human a large portion of the time.<br /> <br /> Maybe the Cell does know. The Vigil is expensive, and that Demon over there is offering you a bump in resources for one of the friends you hang out with, or the girlfriend you were thinking of dumping anyway. Seems like a harmless enough deal.Maybe a little boost from Vampire blood or a leather jacket that is magically bulletproof is sounding really good right now. Hunters compromise a lot. A lot of the Conspiracies use stuff that's not exactly on the up and up. Cheiron uses parts removed from monsters, and the power of the Lucifuge comes straight from Hell. Why shouldn't Cells use what they think they can handle. Part of the game is about where to draw that line between what makes someone a human, and what makes them a monster.<br /> <br /> The biggest thing to rmember though is the agenda of the Supernatural. It's unlikely that they're helping a group of Hunters out of the kindness of their heart. They want something, and the Hunters are tools to achieve that. The Vampire is giving up his rivals, and becoming a bigger threat than they ever were in the process. The Demon likely sees the Hunters as expendable in the fight against the God-Machine. In the end, monsters are allies of convenience, and the group better figure out how they're going to get rid of them t some point, before the monster decides it no longer needs the Hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1279-badger-king","name":"Badger King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1279_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-06T13:06:37-08:00","id":361523,"title":"","content":"Different groups have different viewpoints. Some of the ones I wrote definately have options for supernatural allies. Hakollel shem Hamerkava can be mentors to Promethians and work with Qashmallim. Soci\u00e9t\u00e9 d\u2019Had\u00e8s and The Staff of Janus are both open minded about working with monsters. The Office of the Lord Stewards are diplomats who's entire job is to negociate with monsters. The Ascending Ones do something very similar.<br /> <br /> Basically a Hunter is any mortal who refuses to believe the comforting lie that the supernatural does not exist. That's all it takes, so of course there's plenty of room. Heck, a mortal who's primary ambition is &quot;become a Mage&quot; is absolutely a Hunter.<br /> <br /> In fact I wrote that Mortal, you can find her in Dream Catchers. (Ok, she's heading to become a Hedge Witch, but it's not like she knows the difference or is particularly fussed what kind of mage she becomes)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:21:54-08:00","id":368638,"title":"","content":"Okay another stupid question (I hope not, however). At any rate, I am thinking of playing a game with my cousins, that I before-mentioned elsewhere, where the Oldest Half-Sibling just discovered Mortal &quot;Mysticism&quot; &amp; the youngest half-sibling likes the money working for Vamps can bring him. This is relevant to this topic because because we all want the middle bro to be a bio-kinetic possible recruit for the Hunters. ( He does know anything about the super-natural allies/nature of his siblings). AS Storyteller the Hunter &quot;employers&quot; are going to try exploiting this, they know a little of the oldest &amp; a moderate of the youngest. Depending on the Tier One hunters, how do you think they could/would exploit this. Are there some ways that are not &quot;CANON?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2097-diana-prince","name":"Diana Prince","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T08:57:54-08:00","id":368681,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I follow; did you mean tier three? Tier one hunters generally don't have &quot;employers&quot; to exploit them \u2014 a tier one cell of hunters is just Steve and his bowling team meeting in his garage after they found out a local wizard is rigging the tournament. Tier three is usually where shadowy, malevolent &quot;employers&quot; begin to surface, with some grey area in tier two.<br /> <br /> Hunters are very much not a monolithic community, and how they would try to &quot;exploit&quot; a fellow hunter's supernatural connections depends on the goals and biases of the particular hunter organization. The Field Projects Division hunting monsters for dissection and harvesting by the Cheiron Group is going to have very different compunctions and motivations from a congregation of the Long Night rooting out the influence of Satan in the last days.<br /> <br /> So, I guess, could you rephrase your question? What are you actually meaning to accomplish here, and in the context of what NPC groups, whether in the books or concocted for your personal game?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T09:34:23-08:00","id":368695,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I prob was not clear, obviously. Okay, more info. I planned on the Hunters who &quot;try to&quot; exploit the &quot;Psychic/Gifted&quot; to be Tier One Hunters. They --- whether they work for someone else is not necessary to figure out (in the beginning) unless it makes for good story. I am debating whether to use Witch-Finders/Second Sight for the Magic-User OR for the Psychic/Bio-Kinetic. I would like intrigue for this game (none of my cousins have inter-net access bytheway). The Hunetrs might know a little of the Mystic and obviously figured out the talents of the middle half-bro. They know a lot, but not everything, of the Vamp-associate youngest one. They might have many ideas for the other two, but for some reason really want the middle one on their side for later purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2097-diana-prince","name":"Diana Prince","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:03:46-08:00","id":368708,"title":"","content":"Oh, they'd exploit those abilities like a stereotypical evil corporation would exploit its workforce.<br /> <br /> With <i>extreme</i> prejudice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T10:30:07-08:00","id":368729,"title":"","content":"Cool. Thanks for the info.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2097-diana-prince","name":"Diana Prince","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T14:39:35-08:00","id":378386,"title":"","content":"I would think that most hunters would certainly ally themselves with more humane of human looking supernaturals. Psychics, Hedge-wizards and Mages would certainly work. Especially if they have a common interest or ideals. Changelings could be hit or miss of course. Some hunters if not people, judge solely on appearances sadly. Personally. i prefer the Vanguard and Ascending Ones, who have a stronger understanding of supernaturals and are less likely to backstab or take advantage of there allies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>&quot;I am a daydreamer and a Night thinker.&quot;~</i></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1820-nightout","name":"Nightout","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T17:51:41-08:00","id":378550,"title":"","content":"I think most Hunters care more about immediate threat than human appearance; the first time you watch a human-looking guy tear your buddy's throat out tends to remove any illusions that anyone, no matter how harmless looking, is safe.<br /> <br /> The Vanguard and Ascending Ones aren't <i>stupid</i>; they'll backstab &quot;allies&quot; once they become too dangerous, just like everyone else.<br /> <br /> Really, if you're looking for people with Supernatural allies, the Compacts are your best bet; other than the <i>crazy</i> ones like the Hunt Club, most of them are focused on one kind of Supernatural beastie. The Union is unlikely to care about a monster if it clearly isn't a threat to their neighborhood, the Ashford Abbey is specifically noted as making deals with Supernaturals who can act as suppliers, the Loyalists of Thule don't really care about Monsters that don't build cults around themselves, Network Zero really just want to catch some Supernaturals on film (and hey, there are probably some Supernaturals that would <i>love</i> to get on film - and I'm not talking about nefarious purposes here (though those groups will show up.))<br /> <br /> Gives me an idea for a Hunter chronicle where it's about how Hunters coexist with the Supernatural. Might be neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-23T04:54:18-08:00","id":378895,"title":"","content":"Some monsters have similar goals to hunters. I could see a Union cell and werewolf pack who call the same neighbourhood home deciding to work together, or at least leave each other alone while passing on information about relevant threats - it wouldn't be the most harmonious of relationships, but it's possible. Many sineaters kind of are hunters already - they're suited to dealing with hauntings, and also to figuring out mysterious deaths, while nothing about their nature necessitates preying on humans - I could see more than one cell being eager to work with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T20:51:23-08:00","id":383940,"title":"","content":"It's also distinctly possible for hunters to just have normal ties to the supernatural. I'm currently playing a wolfblooded hunter, for example. There's no reason why they might not have friendly contact with the supernatural before becoming hunters, or before realizing what they were dealing with. What's a hunter to do if they find an old buddy is practicing magic in their spare time? Or that their nephew's a werewolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4777-warkitty","name":"WarKitty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T01:25:17-08:00","id":384052,"title":"","content":"Hunters are human and they will react with the same variation as any other human. Most will fear and react with violence to the supernatural, but they might form the occasional alliance of convenience and they most certainly will be unwitting pawns in the politics of the supernatural. After all, they know little about the supernatural and what mankind does not know, it fears. The violent reaction is made all the more likely since most supernaturals in the World of Darkness are actually evil or at the very least very dangerous to mankind and Hunters simply lack the skill and knowledge to recognize the different factions amongst the supernatural. Would you trust an ogre after just having rescued a bunch of kids from another one that was about to sell them to a Fae? Of course, being human also means that they can and will befriend supernaturals that have proven their trustworthiness although depending on the faction some combinations seem unlikely (vampires befriend the Inquisition springs to mind).<br /> <br /> Another is more whether the supernaturals would want to ally, let alone befriend, with the Hunters. In general mortals are weaker and ill-equipped to deal with the world of the supenaturals. To bring them into your world is exposing them to considerable risk. Of course, you could educate them, but will put them and you at another kind of risk. After all, your fellow supernaturals take a very dim view on revealing their secrets to mortals.<br /> <br /> In short in my campaigns, short term allies of convenience seems very likely to happen, but long term alliances seem extremely unlikely and more a one of a kind thing each with their own unique story and certainly kept private.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-28T11:00:40-08:00","id":384344,"title":"","content":"I have a general story seed about a town where the local Hunter groups and Werewolf packs (there are maybe 2 or 3 of each) have signed a long-term peace agreement. After all, both groups are useful to have around (Hunters might appreciate having muscle that can talk to spirits; Werewolves might appreciate having the Hunters around both as social contact and as intermediaries.)<br /> <br /> Through a quirk of the local Shadow, the agreement is <i>seared</i> into the Codes of local Hunters and Werewolves. Breaking it causes Breaking Points. This wasn't intentional at all, but the advantages (and drawbacks) are becoming steadily more apparent. The Hunters are essentially forming a new Compact, with an eye towards essentially creating a full alliance between Mankind and Werewolfkind.<br /> <br /> Of course, there are large groups on both sides that <i>really</i> don't support this push.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T17:48:36-08:00","id":389159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/358652-is-it-at-all-possible-for-hunters-to-have-supernatural-allies?p=384052#post384052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another is more whether the supernaturals would want to ally, let alone befriend, with the Hunters. In general mortals are weaker and ill-equipped to deal with the world of the supenaturals. To bring them into your world is exposing them to considerable risk. Of course, you could educate them, but will put them and you at another kind of risk. After all, your fellow supernaturals take a very dim view on revealing their secrets to mortals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters are people. Monsters are people when they're not doing monster things. They have goals, and sometimes those goals overlap. Same for personal interests. Friendships both practical and personal can form.<br /> <br /> To dismiss mortals as weaker, physically inferior and therefor unimportant, well... the entire point of HtV is proving that line of thinking to be a mistake. Even beyond that that, mortals provide Touchstones, staff for running businesses in daylight hours, and contacts for providing information. <br /> <br /> The Chronicle I co-run has one Hunter and one Demon troupe. We have members act as &quot;guest stars&quot; in the other side of the Chronicle, which eventually escalated to a marriage between two characters with a child on the way.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2233-agentwestmer","name":"Agentwestmer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2233_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T19:16:48-08:00","id":389250,"title":"","content":"I'm reminded of one of the Conditions in the Overly Specific Conditions PDF they released last year - in particular, the Monster Shares Your Hobby persistent Condition.<br /> <br /> I mean, I know it's <i>supposed</i> to be a joke Condition, but it really works for any Hunter game where monsters aren't KOS.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-02T04:22:21-08:00","id":389658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Agentwestmer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/358652-is-it-at-all-possible-for-hunters-to-have-supernatural-allies?p=389159#post389159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hunters are people. Monsters are people when they're not doing monster things. They have goals, and sometimes those goals overlap. Same for personal interests. Friendships both practical and personal can form.<br /> <br /> To dismiss mortals as weaker, physically inferior and therefor unimportant, well... the entire point of HtV is proving that line of thinking to be a mistake. Even beyond that that, mortals provide Touchstones, staff for running businesses in daylight hours, and contacts for providing information.<br /> <br /> The Chronicle I co-run has one Hunter and one Demon troupe. We have members act as &quot;guest stars&quot; in the other side of the Chronicle, which eventually escalated to a marriage between two characters with a child on the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am not denying that. The intent of my comment was to point out that it is not just a question of what the hunters feel, but also what the 'monsters' want. Monsters know about as much about the Hunters community and their abilities as Hunters know about monsters. Before you as a Storyteller or PC decide an alliance makes sense, don't forget to look at the situation from the opposing view <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-03T13:49:02-08:00","id":391805,"title":"","content":"In my Hunter game I run monsters that are PC leveintelligent if its appropriate. Stupid monsters that are randomly and unpredictably violent don't live long in the World of Darkness before their own kind kill them off for risking exposure for the rest. This creates controversy about dealing with monsters: a Werewolf pack mowed down a group of protesters that a sorcerer had goaded to attack them. There's enough supernatural understanding between the Les Mysteries, Lucifuge and Malleus Maleficarum players that the Hunters know that the mob was possibly supernaturally urged and that the situation was tense and fast paced enough that another solution may not have been in the making. So some players are still advocating d\u00e9tente with this pack. Not all but they are well aware that a straight fight would be a disaster in which several of them would probably be killed and the Werewolves may have some role to play in managing the supernatural ecology. (A role they have cause to question after the Werewolves laughed off attempts to invoke ideas like sympathy for humans plagued by spirits in a tense stand off - they're a Pure pack.) The Les Mysteries player has also uncovered information that these Werewolves are placating an enormously powerful spirit with regular human sacrifice so its a very ethically messy situation. Some of the group agreed to patrol a local hotspot of nasty inter dimensional activity together with the Werewolves to clear their name of some nasty business the Werewolves suspect the Hunters of. Its not a happy situation for anyone but it is an alliance of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1881-the-cowardly-scion","name":"The Cowardly Scion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1881_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-05T11:30:08-08:00","id":393997,"title":"","content":"In short, yes it is possible. The biggest problem is both sides would need a very compelling reason to do so. Consider the hunter's point on view. Most weren't initiated into the World of Darkness by a nice mummy who just woke up and had a good day. No, they get introduced when their best friend forgets their name and after a particularly difficult fight, he punches his bets friend and drywall breaks off of him. Or they come home from a long day at work to find their wife no longer has any blood in her. Hunters usually have problems with making permanent peace with supernaturals because of how they came into their new job. They might come to an uneasy truce or even just a 'no killing each other' policy, but such things would not happen at anything above the cell level, unless you make your own compact, or inferno forbid, conspiracy. Now look at it from the monsters view. How fast does news spread that there is a peaceful, just hunter in the city? Good news never gets around. How fast do you hear a new hunter cell moved in and is beginning to kill your race? It spread like wildfire, as in either everyone knows about it or not a single soul is left alive to spread the news, which is news in and of itself, because bad news does spread. Each side has a large hurdle to jump over before lasting peace could be made, and it shouldn't be anything beyond a cell and a pack/cabal/throng/.....<br /> <br /> While it is possible, it isn't likely. But you can use your ideas to shape how your cell acts. Lets say that your cell has been taking out cabals and all of a sudden, one of your members goes to his Sunday afternoon ritual with his college buddy and discovers he is a mage. Will he grab his salt from his trunk and take him out? Will he tell his cell and try to figure t out from there? Will he confront his friend about it? Will he not tell his cell to protect his friend? You could run with that and cause PLOT to happen. Your hunter is wolf-blooded, right? Did you tell your cell? Do you even know? How would he react to finding out some of his family are werewolves? What about catching one of them in his first change? What about you? What if you turn into a werewolf? How will the cell deal with that? These questions will help define you and your cell of their integrity and their determination. This makes for a less 'bag n tag' story, but a more though provoking chronicle. Try it out, or bring it up to your ST and see if he wants to try a morality hunter chronicle rather than a hunter story.<br /> <br /> I'm letting one of my players run a hunter game and your idea is exactly his. He created a compact called the Kindheart Society where hunters only hunt the monsters who act like monsters and stop other hunters from hurting the &quot;innocent&quot;. Part of the chronicle is deciding where that line is and what you are going to do about it. Meet the gray areas and try to keep your integrity. I'm playing a vampire hunter. It is his sole purpose, but he eventually discovered that a few vampires are just trying to get by, not causing any permanent harm to anybody. He still is not happy about it, but he is trying to hang onto his humanity and let them live. He doesn't trust them or even like them, but he can tolerate their existence. Due to PLOT and my agreement with ST, he became a vampire and now has to deal with his new existence. More stuff to think on instead of pulling out a dragon's breath trench gun and firing away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/13.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4793-hunterinthenight","name":"HunterInTheNight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"168"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T19:09:09-08:00","id":398300,"title":"","content":"My Hunter character IS a Sin-Eater (he became one after I'd been playing him for three years already). He works closely with the local werewolf pack; they help him keep an eye on things. His main apprentice hunter is an Obrimos mage. My hunter loves working with mages, magic is such an amazingly useful tool to have at one's disposal. The only kind of &quot;monster&quot; he's really prejudiced against is vampires, but he'll even cooperate with them if the need is great enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2573-inkpenavenger","name":"inkpenavenger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2573_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-03T18:40:42-08:00","id":427216,"title":"","content":"I'd say that, unless a Cell happens to have a particularly unyielding &quot;if it ain't human, we kills it, no exceptions&quot; policy, alliances with supers would be natural, provided said supers were of compatible mindsets.<br /> <br /> In particular, I can see Sin-Eaters of a more benevolent bent being amenable to helping out Hunters in a struggle against restless ghosts; Uratha cooperating to end a spirit incursion; high-Humanity Vampires participating in ... well, a coup against other Vampires, most likely; Changelings coming to Hunters for help when servants of the True Fae come a-knocking, if they're out of options; A Promethean might enlist Hunter assistance against a Hundred-Handed ...<br /> <br /> You get the idea. Story hooks a-plenty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5158-xenu-s-paradox","name":"Xenu's Paradox","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"212"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T05:45:09-08:00","id":427638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xenu's Paradox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/358652-is-it-at-all-possible-for-hunters-to-have-supernatural-allies?p=427216#post427216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that, unless a Cell happens to have a particularly unyielding &quot;if it ain't human, we kills it, no exceptions&quot; policy, alliances with supers would be natural, provided said supers were of compatible mindsets.<br /> <br /> In particular, I can see Sin-Eaters of a more benevolent bent being amenable to helping out Hunters in a struggle against restless ghosts; Uratha cooperating to end a spirit incursion; high-Humanity Vampires participating in ... well, a coup against other Vampires, most likely; Changelings coming to Hunters for help when servants of the True Fae come a-knocking, if they're out of options; A Promethean might enlist Hunter assistance against a Hundred-Handed ...<br /> <br /> You get the idea. Story hooks a-plenty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously, each gaming group depicts the worlds in the way that group prefers, but I always got the impression that at its core virtually all NPCs (and certainly organizations) within the WoD have rather uncompromising inflexbile and intollerant views on the world. It fits both the darkness of the world as well as creating interesting stories, since ultimately conflict is what drives story. As such I would generally treat every cell of Hunters (and the supernatural groups for that matter) as being particularly unyielding until proven wrong by the PCs. I certainly sometimes have to remind my players that they might be well aware of the intricities of e.g. Werewolf society, all their characters know about it, is how those creatures are depicted in books and movies which is mostly as murderous maneaters influenced by the moon who can appear to be very humane and friendly during the day. So yes, on paper cooperation makes a lot of sense because we as readers see a lot more of the picture than any inhabitant of the WoD ever does. In practice I would consider it being extremely rare, one of a kind situations specific to a particular situation and more often than not after hard work by one or more PCs <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T14:20:49-08:00","id":428122,"title":"","content":"Changelings and Geists in particular can be fairly amenable to a teamup. <br /> <br /> Changeling and Hunter are my two favorite lines, so I like coming up with ways to mix them...<br /> <br /> One of the big things about Changelings is that they aren't just capable of having positive relations with humans, but if you want to keep high clarity, it's basically essential. (And by &quot;positive&quot;, I mean symbiotic, cooperative, both-sides-wish-for-the-best-for-each-other type relationships.) They don't drink blood or have dangerous hunts or socially disruptive claims on locii to gain energy. A changeling can harvest entirely from the hedge, pledges, or dreams without having any apparent negative effect on human society, and even an emotion harvest is only harmful when someone is careless enough to overtly harm, terrorize, or seduce just for the glamour. Most &quot;good&quot; changelings get along with humanity and want to protect it in general, and the fae creatures they are instinctively aligned against (hedgebeasts, privateers, clarity-bankrupt changelings that are a danger to everyone around them, Gentry) are generally harmful to humanity as a whole.<br /> <br /> Hunters are ironically potentially a Changeling's best friend. They know about the supernatural, so you only have to hide the parts of your supernatural life you have sworn to keep in confidence (and can simply say &quot;I swore not to reveal that&quot;,) they tend to carry weapons, including cold iron weapons, and could be a handy way to beat back a True Fae, and you would generally have a pretty good idea that they'd be just as opposed to privateers and True Fae as you are. Compacts and conspiracies can also help with forging documents to get you a new life. <br /> <br /> Changelings, meanwhile, have a lot to offer if kept friendly. Magic healing is an obvious one - Warmth of Blood works wonders, and Faerie Healing or Burden of Life (if the changeling is willing to risk taking on the damage of a comrade in active combat) would easily keep hunters on the vigil, and out of the morgue. They also have access to loads of information-gathering magic. Many types of changelings can just use kenning or 1-dot contracts to see all sorts of supernatural stuff, and onieromancy and supernatural research lets them suss out difficult-to-find banes for fighting other supernaturals. Any hunter who trusts a changeling deeply enough to let them in would also be able to benefit from the dreamshaping of a changeling. A changeling psychologist could use onieromancy to help ease the traumas of the vigil, and scour nightmares into healing dreams or willpower dreams. (I like having house rules for onieromancy making morality protection/recovery easier.)<br /> <br /> The biggest problem would be keeping Hunters seeing the difference between the &quot;good guys&quot; and &quot;bad guys&quot; of the fae world. It's not like you can whip out your character sheet and prove you've got high clarity, (except for that one Malleus Mallificarum thing that lets you outright see a person's morality) and even if you could prove it, there isn't any proof it won't plummet. And of course, the only changeling most people see are the ones that blow their clarity and start doing reckless stuff in public. Fetches are an especially difficult sticking point, as murdering a stick-man that looks human can be just as disruptive to society as murdering a real human... which is all the more reason changelings need to think carefully about just shooting fetches by reflex. An aware fetch could easily get on a hunter's good side, as well. Changelings more willing to work with non-hostile fetches would probably go further working with Hunters.<br /> <br /> Mortal Remains also overtly mentions that some compacts and conspiracies are friendly to Changelings in general:<br /> <br /> VALKYRIE doesn't overtly work with changelings, but they see them as a threat to national security only in individual cases, not as a group, and they happily supply them forged documents. Simply telling VALKYRIE you're still an American citizen and still love your country, and want to help stop the threat of vampires or whatever as much as they do, and can supply information, access to goblin markets and the hedge if need be could easily result in at least a small-scale alliance. Besides, privateers are a direct threat to humanity, so VALKYRIE could help fight a changeling's fights for them, and still chalk it up as a win. You could potentially even have a whole freehold inside a VALKYRIE base made up of ex-military or other government employees who simply turned themselves in to their superiors when they escaped the hedge after being abducted while in the line of duty. (I remember Dogs of War also had something similar, but with werewolves...) <br /> <br /> The Union is potentially capable of letting changelings ally with them simply because they share common goals: Having a secure neighborhood for their families. Ogres and Wizened may have a deeper connection to the blue-collared types of the Union, as well, and may well be co-workers with the hunters. Just so long as they prove stable, and they can help point out the real threats, then only the fetch and attempts to blend back in with their old lives might cause turmoil. <br /> <br /> Ascending Order outright states in its section that they deal with changelings, if not officially, for bits and parts of hedge beasts and hedge fruit to make potions from. In fact, the biggest point of contention may be how ethical and patient the AO is: If they want to strangle their golden goose to cook it up for another of their potions, instead of relying upon the changeling to lay down their golden hedge fruits. <br /> <br /> The Lucifuge and Malleus Mallificarum officially don't care about fae, or at least, don't see them as major threats. It's not hard to see one that has something to offer striking up a short-term alliance of convenience that might grow into a longer-term one... if the Changelings are VERY careful to keep proving they are trustworthy, of course. A Catholic changeling in particular might have success with some Malleus Mallificarum cells from cultures that have folkloric traditions of heroic fae. If the changeling takes mass, confesses their sins, and helps take the fight to the Devil, and says it's all to regain their soul that was scourged by the demons beyond the hedge, that may well be enough to prove they're on the right side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-04T15:31:08-08:00","id":428221,"title":"","content":"For Geists: (I'm going to try making this one shorter...)<br /> <br /> It depends upon the motivation of the Sin-Eater, of course, but if you're playing a sort of &quot;homicide detective that talks to ghosts&quot; type, you could probably make a few friends among the living. <br /> <br /> A few obvious ones pop out:<br /> <br /> Loyalists of Thule want to explore the Underworld, and are willing to hire Sin-Eaters on as guides. It's just a matter of finding one who'd be willing to lead a band of potential red shirts down onto the alien planet...<br /> <br /> NetZo loves filming ghosts. Sin-Eaters want ghosts to get messages out to the living. The only difficulty is keeping NetZo from prying too much into the Sin-Eater's affairs. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5120-wraith_magus","name":"Wraith_Magus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}